# SSi Learner Profile — motivation layer as built
# AI Projects Markup Language (APML)

metadata:
  title: "Learner Profile / Mirror / Portrait"
  version: "1.1.0"
  date: "2026-08-03"
  last_updated: "2026-08-19 — A-176: the explainer is diagram-led and the diagram is the player's own phase pill; the streaks copy now states our choice honestly, without a claim we cannot know and without an opinion about anyone else's app"
  author: "SSi Team"
  status: "preview — shipped to dev on the unlinked /me route"
  source: "founder design session 2026-08-03"
  supersedes: "apml/design/gamification-philosophy.apml (its MECHANICS; its principles stand)"

# =============================================================================
# WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY THE OLD SPEC IS ONLY HALF DEAD
# =============================================================================

ruling SupersedesGamificationMechanics:
  date: "2026-08-03"
  kept_from_the_old_spec:
    - "Show the results of good behaviour, hide the mechanics"
    - "Celebrate returns, never guilt absences"
    - "Overjustification: external rewards destroy intrinsic motivation"
    - "No streaks, no full leaderboards, no explicit achievements"
  overturned_from_the_old_spec:
    visible_points_per_cycle: "DELETED — no incentive points anywhere"
    evolution_score: "DELETED — replaced by the portrait, which is an estimate, not a score"
    top_5_leaderboard: "DELETED — comparison is not the instrument"
    percentile: "DELETED"
    contribution_counter: "not built; collective purpose is not this surface's job"
  rationale: |
    The old spec kept a points economy and only hid its formula. The 2026-08-03
    ruling goes further: numbers exist ONLY as descriptive insights the learner
    could count themselves — goes, minutes, milliseconds. A hidden formula still
    survives, but it produces an ESTIMATE OF WHERE THEY ARE, never a reward.

# =============================================================================
# THE THREE LAYERS
# =============================================================================

layer CelebrateAdherence:
  energy: "dog, not dentist"
  rewarded_thing: "showing up and giving it a go — the only one"
  vocabulary:
    speaking_opportunity: "a GO — never 'opportunity', never 'attempt'"
  surfaces:
    - "goes this week (hero number)"
    - "speaking minutes / listening minutes this week"
  never:
    - "any mention of absence, in any form"
    - "streaks, days-since, missed days, lapses"
  invariant: |
    ABSENCE IS NOT REPRESENTABLE. The payload has no key that can carry a
    streak, a gap or a days-since count. This is enforced by test, not by
    discipline — api/me/profile.test.ts and views/me/ProfileView.test.ts.

layer ReflectExecution:
  name: "the mirror"
  reports: "how quickly replies come — directly, honestly, UNREWARDED"
  under_the_hood: "the envelope signals stay under the hood, never surfaced"
  framing: "where you are x the direction you're moving"
  first_30_hours_job: |
    ACCELERATING EXTRAPOLATION — show the curve early, before the learner can
    feel it, so belief outruns doubt. Hence the dashed projection, drawn at
    HALF the observed slope: an over-promise that fails to land would cost the
    exact trust this panel exists to build.
  honesty_rule: "a flat line is stated plainly; no invented progress"

layer EstimateLevel:
  name: "the portrait"
  formula: "difficulty x execution, where COURSE POSITION is the difficulty term"
  why_position_dominates: |
    Brilliant on the third thing you ever learned is not expert. Struggling on
    the nine-hundredth is not weak. Execution may nudge the estimate by one
    rung; it can never carry it. Pinned by test.
  surfaced_as: "a notional CEFR band with an interval that visibly narrows"
  never: "a test result; a pass/fail; a score"
  confidence: "from sample volume, saturating — the interval collapses as it settles"

# =============================================================================
# THE PLAN
# =============================================================================

system ReasonablePlan:
  unit: "30 HOURS — fixed"
  free_variable: "cadence"
  metaphors: "fast x hard / slow x easy / going up the mountain"
  routes:
    - "a real burn — 6 hours a day, 5 days"
    - "an hour a day — 30 days"
    - "weekends only — 3 hours a day, both days, five weekends"
    - "half an hour a day — 60 days"
    - "a gentle quarter hour — 15 minutes a day, 120 days"
  honest_note: |
    The gentlest-sounding route is the HARDEST to hold — most decision points,
    least evidence per sitting. Said warmly, and never as a reason to shame
    anyone who picks it.
  learner_job_thereafter: "press play. That is the whole ask."
  persistence: "localStorage key ssi-plan-cadence — no server write, no new table"

# =============================================================================
# MODE PHASING — the routines
# =============================================================================

system ModePhasing:
  principle: "MAINTAIN focus, CHANGE routines. The focus is the language; the routine is the mode."
  modes: ["speaking", "listening", "drills", "immersion"]
  arc:
    zero_to_thirty_hours: "mostly speaking, listening folded in"
    thirty_to_hundred_hours: "increasingly bulk listening deep dives on harder material"
  surfaced_as: "a nudge in the dog voice — bring the right ball. Never a score, never a correction."

# =============================================================================
# THE EXPLAINERS
# =============================================================================

system Explainers:
  mechanic: "pulse-until-viewed, reused verbatim from the schools/orgs How-this-works"
  independence: "the two sections carry independent seen-state"
  how_this_works:
    covers: "using the app — what pressing play does, what a go is, the modes, changing course"
    pulse: "RED (the existing flavour)"
  why_this_works:
    covers: "the methodology — the 30-hour arc, mode phasing, why no streaks or points, the evidence since 2009"
    pulse: "BLUE (app-update / Alexander blue)"
  thirty_hour_promise:
    lives: "inside Why-this-works, and NOWHERE else"
    not: "a headline — we are not a claims-focused company"
    claim:
      - "you will be getting into conversations"
      - "you will be moving towards more listening work"
      - "you will be noticing how much surfaces easily that was genuinely impossible before"
    instrument: "the mirror quietly shows these predictions coming true — prediction fulfilled is the anti-doubt instrument"

# =============================================================================
# LAWS
# =============================================================================

law LanguageWall:
  rule: "Internal and non-self-evident technical terminology is NEVER learner-facing"
  banned_on_learner_surfaces: ["LEGO", "Script", "VAD", "prosody", "adherence", "SEED", "latency"]
  say_instead: ["a go", "the thing you just said", "how quickly it comes", "listening deep dives"]
  enforcement: "asserted against the RENDERED text in ProfileView.test.ts"

law PositionIsContent:
  rule: |
    Position is shown as the learner's OWN WORDS — the last thing they said, in
    both languages. Never a number, never an internal unit id.

law NumbersAreDescriptive:
  rule: "Every visible number is one the learner could count themselves"
  allowed: ["goes", "minutes", "hours", "milliseconds", "days they chose"]
  forbidden: ["points", "score", "XP", "rank", "percentile", "multiplier"]
  hidden_formula: "server-side only, in api/me/profile.ts — never shipped to the client"

law HonestSourcing:
  rule: "Each block carries its own source tag; sample data is labelled as sample data"

# =============================================================================
# IMPLEMENTATION
# =============================================================================

implementation:
  route: "/me — UNLINKED from every nav, which IS the flag"
  server: "api/me/profile.ts (+ profile.test.ts)"
  client_reader: "composables/useLearnerProfile.ts"
  view: "views/me/ProfileView.vue (+ ProfileView.test.ts)"
  panels:
    - "components/me/AdherencePanel.vue"
    - "components/me/MirrorPanel.vue"
    - "components/me/PortraitPanel.vue"
    - "components/me/PlanPanel.vue"
    - "components/me/HowThisWorksLearner.vue"
    - "components/me/WhyThisWorks.vue"
    - "components/me/CourseSwitchRow.vue"
    - "components/me/SettingsDirection.vue"
    - "components/me/CyclePillFigure.vue"
  content: "explainer/learnerExplainers.ts"
  throb: "explainer/learnerThrob.ts — learner-side sibling of howThisWorksThrob.ts, which is untouched"

# =============================================================================
# THE EXPLAINER FIGURE — A-176, founder ruling 2026-08-19
# =============================================================================

ruling DiagramLedExplainer:
  date: "2026-08-19"
  founder_words: "A is best - diagram led, but I wonder if we should use the graphic from the actual player to illustrate"
  decision: |
    The "What pressing play does" block is illustrated, and the illustration is
    the player's OWN phase pill — same shape, same four icons, same 20/40/20/20
    proportions, same red. The picture in the explainer and the pill on the
    player screen teach each other; an invented graphic would teach neither.
  component: "components/me/CyclePillFigure.vue"
  mechanism: |
    ExplainerBlock gains an optional `figure` field naming an illustration.
    Prose stays in explainer/learnerExplainers.ts, pixels stay in the component
    — the existing separation, extended rather than broken.
  deliberate_duplication: |
    CyclePillFigure DUPLICATES the player's markup rather than sharing it. The
    live pill in LearningPlayer.vue is interactive and carries a long bug
    history in its CSS comments — sticky iOS hover, the invisible-countdown
    track, the pointer-events pass-through. Fifty static lines is the cheaper
    and safer trade than refactoring load-bearing playback chrome.
  inert_by_construction: "divs not buttons, no handlers, pill aria-hidden behind one sentence of alt text in learner words; nothing animates"
  labels: "learner language only — 'you hear it', 'your turn', 'then twice, properly'; never PROMPT / SPEAK / VOICE_1"

ruling HonestAboutWhatWeKnow:
  date: "2026-08-19"
  founder_words: "we don't want to mislead - the app DOES timestamp every session, so we DO know how long has elapsed since the previous session. we just don't use streaks because they create pressure and we want this journey to be fun"
  corrects: "the earlier acceptance_test below, which asserted the system CANNOT know about an absence"
  rule: |
    The system CAN know. Every session is timestamped, which is how the app
    resumes where the learner left off. The law is not ignorance, it is
    restraint: that timestamp is never surfaced, never counted into a run of
    days, and never used to push. Copy that claims we cannot know is a lie and
    fails the build.
  and_no_snippiness: |
    Founder, same message: "we don't want to be snippy about what other apps do,
    and why streaks are bad". The copy states OUR choice and OUR reason. A
    reader must not be able to tell we hold an opinion about anyone else's app —
    no comparison, no argument against streaks, warmth only.
  thirty_hours_honestly: |
    Founder: "it's tough for the first 30 hours but then it really does get a
    lot easier". Both halves, neither oversold. Still inside Why this works,
    still never a headline.
  enforced_in: "explainer/learnerExplainers.test.ts"

acceptance_test:
  fixture: "the anti-gallery — six real Duolingo shame emails"
  rule: |
    Nothing in this design could ever generate any of them. Every one of those
    emails needs the system to know about an absence — and per
    HonestAboutWhatWeKnow the system DOES know, because sessions are
    timestamped. So the guarantee is a product law rather than a data-model
    accident: nothing on any learner surface reads, counts or acts on that gap,
    and no copy may claim we are unable to.
